eusoilvoc:ModifiedUniversalSoilLossEquation a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader eusoilvoc:SoilErosionModels ;
    skos:definition [ dcterms:source agrovoc:c_55f2905b ;
            rdf:value "MUSLE is a modification of the Universal Soil Loss Equation (USLE). MUSLE is similar to USLE except for the energy component. USLE depends strictly upon rainfall as the source of erosive energy. MUSLE uses storm-based runoff volumes and runoff peak flows to simulate erosion and sediment yield (Williams 1995). The use of runoff variables rather than rainfall erosivity as the driving force enables MUSLE to estimate sediment yields for individual storm events."@en ] ;
    skos:exactMatch agrovoc:c_55f2905b ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/eusoilvoc> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Modified Universal Soil Loss Equation"@en .

